### Wasil API End-to-End Scenario Script
# Execute these requests sequentially from top to bottom to verify the complete order lifecycle.

@host = http://localhost:5247
@customerId = 1
@addressId = 1
@storeId = 1
@productId = 1
@orderId = 1

### Step 1: Create a Customer
POST {{host}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Integration",
  "lastName": "Tester",
  "email": "integration.tester@wasil.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0791234567"
}

### Step 2: Add an Address for the Customer
POST {{host}}/api/v1/customers/{{customerId}}/addresses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "street": "100 Main St",
  "city": "Amman",
  "zipCode": "11190"
}

### Step 3: Search Products (Find Store and Product)
# Note the storeId and productId returned in the response items.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?text=milk&page=1&pageSize=5

### Step 4: Place an Order
# Make sure customerId, storeId, and addressId match existing records.
# Product must belong to the specified store.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "storeId": {{storeId}},
  "addressId": {{addressId}},
  "paymentMethod": 0,
  "lines": [
    {
      "productId": {{productId}},
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Step 5: Get Order Details (Check initial Pending status)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### Step 6a: Update Status to Accepted (1)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 1
}

### Step 6b: Update Status to Preparing (2)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 2
}

### Step 6c: Update Status to OutForDelivery (3)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 3
}

### Step 6d: Update Status to Delivered (4)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 4
}

### Step 7: Get Order Details Again (Verify complete status logs)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### Step 8: Get Store Dashboard (Verify metrics reflect the completed order)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/dashboard/{{storeId}}
